th 6\n","|   |   |   |--- digi_C1c >  2.50\n","|   |   |   |   |--- truncated branch of depth 8\n","|   |   |--- conf_B2 >  3.50\n","|   |   |   |--- Digital_x_Training <= 0.29\n","|   |   |   |   |--- truncated branch of depth 12\n","|   |   |   |--- Digital_x_Training >  0.29\n","|   |   |   |   |--- truncated branch of depth 5\n","\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x1200 with 4 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 2000x1000 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 0 Axes>"]},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","Top-level splitting features and thresholds:\n","Node 0: train_E7 < 2.50\n","Node 1: Digital_x_Training < 0.09\n","Node 2: res_D4 < 2.50\n","Node 3: train_E7 < 1.50\n","Node 4: conf_B2 < 2.50\n","\n","Final Baseline Models Comparison:\n","        Model      R2   RMSE\n","        Dummy -0.0863 1.8578\n","          MLR  0.9699 0.3086\n","        Lasso  0.9699 0.3086\n","        Ridge  0.9699 0.3086\n","Decision Tree  0.7303 0.9254\n"]},{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["['../outputs/models/04_dt_model.pkl']"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":11}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Key Insights from Final Baseline Comparison\n","\n","**1. Linear Models Dominate Performance**\n","**Modelling** results across the different architectures show that linear models (MLR, Lasso, and Ridge) achieve an exceptionally high ****. This indicates that teacher readiness is highly predictable through a linear combination of the individual items. The **Decision Tree** performance () is respectable but significantly lower, suggesting that the underlying relationships in the data are predominantly linear rather than characterized by complex non-linear interactions.\n","\n","**2. Divergent Feature Importance**\n","The models highlight different priorities depending on their mathematical structure:\n","\n","* **MLR/Lasso/Ridge Hierarchy:** These models prioritize **Professional Confidence** (conf_B2, conf_B6) and **Digital Skills** (digi_C1c, digi_C1d, digi_C2e) as the primary drivers of the index.\n","* **Decision Tree Hierarchy:** This model identifies **Training Quality** (train_E7) and the **Digital-Training Interaction** as the most significant splitting criteria, providing a different perspective on how variables segment the population.\n","\n","**3. Critical Policy Findings and Thresholds**\n","**Visualizing** the implications for policy through these models reveals three major takeaways:\n","\n","| Finding | Policy Implication |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| **Confidence is the strongest predictor** | Prioritize programs that boost teacher self-efficacy. |\n","| **Digital skills are secondary drivers** | Implement targeted digital literacy training. |\n","| **Quality > Attendance** | Invest in high-quality training content rather than focusing on attendance metrics. |\n","\n","The **Decision Tree** specifically identifies a critical threshold at **train_E7 < 2.5**. This represents a \"tipping point\" where readiness scores drop significantly, marking a specific area for targeted intervention."],"metadata":{"id":"dEYZrePt_p9R"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Compiling all baseline results to provide a comprehensive performance overview\n","results_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Model': ['Dummy (Mean)', 'Multiple Linear Regression', 'Lasso', 'Ridge', 'Decision Tree'],\n","    'R2 (CV)': [-0.0863, 0.9699, 0.9699, 0.9699, 0.7303],\n","    'RMSE (CV)': [1.8578, 0.3086, None, 0.3086, 0.9254],\n","    'MAE (CV)': [1.4797, 0.2448, None, None, None],\n","    'Features Used': [0, 19, 18, 19, 19],\n","    'Interpretability': ['Very High', 'High', 'High', 'High', 'Very High'],\n","    'Non-linear Captured': ['No', 'No', 'No', 'No', 'Yes']\n","})\n","\n","print(\"\\nComprehensive Results Table:\")\n","print(results_summary.to_string(index=False))\n","results_summary.to_csv('../outputs/tables/04_all_baselines_comparison.csv', index=False)\n","\n","#Import cross_val_predict for statistical comparison\n","from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_predict\n","\n","#Conducting statistical comparison using the Diebold-Mariano test to assess error differences\n","print(\"\\nGenerating cross-validated predictions for statistical comparison...\")\n","\n","#Modelling predictions for each baseline architecture\n","dummy_pred = cross_val_predict(DummyRegressor(strategy='mean'), X_train, y_train, cv=group_kfold, groups=groups_train)\n","mlr_pred = cross_val_predict(LinearRegression(), X_train, y_train, cv=group_kfold, groups=groups_train)\n","ridge_pred = cross_val_predict(Ridge(alpha=5.9948, random_state=42), X_train, y_train, cv=group_kfold, groups=groups_train)\n","dt_pred = cross_val_predict(DecisionTreeRegressor(max_depth=None, min_samples_leaf=2, min_samples_split=5, random_state=42), X_train, y_train, cv=group_kfold, groups=groups_train)\n","\n","errors = {\n","    'Dummy': y_train - dummy_pred,\n","    'MLR': y_train - mlr_pred,\n","    'Ridge': y_train - ridge_pred,\n","    'Tree': y_train - dt_pred\n","}\n","\n","def dm_test(errors1, errors2):\n","    d = errors1**2 - errors2**2\n","    d_mean = np.mean(d)\n","    d_std = np.std(d, ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(d))\n","    dm_stat = d_mean / d_std\n","    p_value = 2 * (1 - stats.norm.cdf(abs(dm_stat)))\n","    return dm_stat, p_value\n","\n","#Printing statistical significance results\n","print(\"\\nDiebold-Mariano Test Results (comparing squared errors):\")\n","for model in ['MLR', 'Ridge', 'Tree']:\n","    dm_stat, p_val = dm_test(errors['Dummy'], errors[model])\n","    print(f\"{model} vs Dummy: DM={dm_stat:.4f}, p={p_val:.4f}\")\n","\n","#Visualizing model performance metrics and prediction distributions\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n","\n","#Comparing R2 scores across all models\n","models_plot = ['Dummy', 'MLR', 'Lasso', 'Ridge', 'Tree']\n","r2_values = [-0.0863, 0.9699, 0.9699, 0.9699, 0.7303]\n","axes[0, 0].bar(models_plot, r2_values, color=['red' if x < 0 else 'green' for x in r2_values], edgecolor='black')\n","axes[0, 0].set_title('Model Performance Comparison (R2)')\n","axes[0, 0].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n","\n","#Comparing RMSE to assess error magnitudes\n","rmse_values = [1.8578, 0.3086, 0, 0.3086, 0.9254]\n","axes[0, 1].bar(models_plot, rmse_values, color='skyblue', edgecolor='black')\n","axes[0, 1].set_title('Model Performance Comparison (RMSE)')\n","\n","#Visualizing agreement between linear and non-linear predictions\n","axes[1, 0].scatter(mlr_pred, dt_pred, alpha=0.5, edgecolors='black')\n","axes[1, 0].plot([mlr_pred.min(), mlr_pred.max()], [mlr_pred.min(), mlr_pred.max()], 'r--', label='Perfect agreement')\n","axes[1, 0].set_title('MLR vs Decision Tree Predictions')\n","\n","#Modelling residual distributions to verify error normality\n","axes[1, 1].hist(errors['MLR'], bins=30, alpha=0.5, label='MLR', edgecolor='black')\n","axes[1, 1].hist(errors['Tree'], bins=30, alpha=0.5, label='Tree', edgecolor='black')\n","axes[1, 1].set_title('Residual Distributions: MLR vs Tree')\n","axes[1, 1].legend()\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig('../outputs/figures/04_final_comparison.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n","plt.show()\n","\n","#Finalizing findings and archiving recommendations for advanced modelling in Notebook 05\n","with open('../outputs/tables/04_baseline_summary.txt', 'w') as f:\n","    f.write(\"BASELINE MODELS SUMMARY\\n\" + \"=\"*50 + \"\\n\")\n","    f.write(results_summary.to_string() + \"\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"1. MLR achieves R2 = 0.9699 - relationships are primarily linear\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"2. Confidence and Digital skills are strongest predictors\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"3. Training quality > attendance\\n\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"933RfUFb_q9b","exe